meta {
  name: get_effective_ims_profile
  type: http
  seq: 156
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/ims/lines/{{line_id}}/profile
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
}

docs {
  cellular_ims.bearer and vowifi_ims.bearer are optional safe configuration metadata:
  authentication.method, username_present/password_present flags (never values),
  pcscf_via_pco, pcscf_via_dhcp, source and optional validation_error.
  These requirements do not claim adapter support or current registration readiness.

  Credential write intent (authenticated API only):
  PATCH /api/ims/lines/{line_id}/override uses ims_cellular.bearer / ims_vowifi.bearer.
  Omission preserves the stored policy only at the unchanged SIM/profile/APN binding;
  explicit null clears the whole override (inherits catalog), and a complete policy
  object replaces it atomically. Redacted PAP/CHAP responses are invalid replacements.
  Both username and password must be supplied for PAP/CHAP replacement; missing and
  deliberately empty password are different. WiFi rejects cellular bearer requirements.

  PUT /api/vowifi/carrier-profiles similarly treats omitted ims.bearer as unchanged,
  null as reset to default, and a full object as replacement. An editor carrying a
  non-default redacted policy also sends ims.bearer_unchanged=true, requiring an
  existing database record at the same profile/PLMN/APN; this rejects accidental
  credential removal when copying a catalog record or changing the profile id.
  Do not send bearer_unchanged together with an explicit bearer replacement/clear.
  Private storage retains credentials; detail/list/write/status responses never do.
}
